--- Finding (draw_a_rotating_cube): a record named like a type the generated Rust
--- uses does not build compiled. `struct Vec` shadows Rust's `Vec`, which the
--- emitted `CrowResult` (`trace: Vec<String>`) names.
---
--- crow run -i: prints 3.
--- crow run:
---   error[E0107]: struct takes 0 generic arguments but 1 generic argument was supplied
---     --> src/main.rs:10:12
---   error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused what Crow
---   accepted, a bug in Crow, not in this program (`crow run -i` runs it meanwhile)
--- Expected: 3 in both modes (the record's name renamed out of Rust's way, as
--- rust_names.rs does for the names Rust reserves).
---
--- The same with other names (each `struct T [x, y]` / `p = T[1, 2]` / `log[p.x + p.y]`):
---   String      error[E0053]: method `crow_repr` has an incompatible type for trait
---   BTreeMap    error[E0255]: the name `BTreeMap` is defined multiple times
---   CrowResult  error[E0428]: the name `CrowResult` is defined multiple times
---   Clone       error[E0404]: expected trait, found struct `Clone`
---   Self        error: expected identifier, found keyword `Self`
--- (Option, Box, Some, Ok, Result, HashMap, Default, Fn and CrowTensor build.)
--- The same class for a function named like the emitter's own helpers
--- (`fn crow_stop[x]` / `return x + 1` / `log[crow_stop[41]]`, likewise
--- `crow_trace_push`): 42 interpreted; compiled
---   error[E0428]: the name `crow_stop` is defined multiple times
--- (a function named main, drop, std, core, rayon, crow_runtime, alloc, vec,
--- format or panic builds.)

struct Vec [x, y]

p = Vec[1, 2]
log[p.x + p.y]
